///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470706///

UPDATE: ALL CONTAMINATED SOIL HAS BEEN CLEANED UP AND ALL EQUIPMENT HAS BEEN WIPED DOWN. NO CHANGE TO THE AMOUNT OF RELEASED MATERIAL.

ORIGINAL: CALLER REPORTED THAT AT 0715, THE OPS TEAM WAS ON SITE AND IDENTIFIED .5 INCH LEAK ON A PUMP AT THE PIPELINE STATION. 50 GALLONS OF CRUDE OIL RELEASED ONTO SOIL AND ONTO THE EQUIPMENT ITSELF. NO WATERWAY IMPACTS HAVE BEEN REPORTED. IT IS UNKNOWN TO THE CALLER IF ANY DAMAGES HAVE OCCURRED AT THIS TIME.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC 1461720///

UPDATE: THE BARGE CONTAINS TWO STAINLESS STEEL TWO 250-300 GALLON TOTES. IT IS UNKNOWN THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL INSIDE EITHER. ONE TOTE HAS A UN 1203 (GASOLINE) PLACARD ON THE SIDE. THE OTHER TOTE HAS A UN 1230 (METHANOL) PLACARD. ADDITIONALLY THE BARGE HAS THREE 55 GALLON DRUMS LABELED AS HAVING NON-HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCE (UNSPECIFIED). ONE OF THESE HAS DRIED OIL ON IT. THE BARGE ITSELF HAS TWO OIL STORAGE COMPARTMENTS THAT ARE CONFIRMED TO HAVE AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF CRUDE OIL IN THEM. THE CALLER DID NOT CONFIRM IF ANY OF THESE MATERIALS HAS RELEASED.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY DISCOVERED A BARGE WITH MULTIPLE TOTES AND BARRELS CONTAINING VARIOUS MATERIALS. THE CALLER SUSPECTS THAT SOME OF THE CONTAINERS ARE LEAKING ONTO THE BARGE.  THE CALLER SUSPECTS THAT THE BARGE IS SITTING ON THE BOTTOM. CURRENTLY MATERIAL HAS RELEASED FROM THE BARGE INTO AN OIL CANAL OFF OF THE GULF CANAL.

///THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1470627///

REPORT IS BEING CORRECTED FROM POTENTIAL TO ACTUAL, AS SOME OF THE MATERIALS (POTASSIUM CHLORIDE, DIESEL) HAVE ACTUALLY RELEASED.

ORGINAL:
///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC 1461720///

UPDATE: THE BARGE CONTAINS TWO STAINLESS STEEL TWO 250-300 GALLON TOTES. IT IS UNKNOWN THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL INSIDE EITHER. ONE TOTE HAS A UN 1203 (GASOLINE) PLACARD ON THE SIDE. THE OTHER TOTE HAS A UN 1230 (METHANOL) PLACARD. ADDITIONALLY THE BARGE HAS THREE 55 GALLON DRUMS LABELED AS HAVING NON-HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCE (UNSPECIFIED). ONE OF THESE HAS DRIED OIL ON IT. THE BARGE ITSELF HAS TWO OIL STORAGE COMPARTMENTS THAT ARE CONFIRMED TO HAVE AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF CRUDE OIL IN THEM. THE CALLER DID NOT CONFIRM IF ANY OF THESE MATERIALS HAS RELEASED.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY DISCOVERED A BARGE WITH MULTIPLE TOTES AND BARRELS CONTAINING VARIOUS MATERIALS. THE CALLER SUSPECTS THAT SOME OF THE CONTAINERS ARE LEAKING ONTO THE BARGE.  THE CALLER SUSPECTS THAT THE BARGE IS SITTING ON THE BOTTOM. CURRENTLY MATERIAL HAS RELEASED FROM THE BARGE INTO A OIL CANAL OFF OF THE GULF CANAL.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470653///

UPDATE: THE SUSPECTED RESPONSIBLE PARTY INFORMATION HAS BEEN UPDATED. INCIDENT TIME HAS BEEN UPDATED. AMOUNT OF MATERIAL RELEASED HAS BEEN UPDATED TO 65 MCF. CALLER REPORTED THAT THE OPERATOR OF THE LAWNMOWER IS THE INDIVIDUAL WHO RECEIVED UNSPECIFIED INJURIES.  FIRE INVOLVED AND FIRE EXTINGUISHED HAVE BEEN UPDATED TO YES. MEDIA INTEREST HAS BEEN UPDATED TO LOW. RELEASE RATE WAS UPDATED TO 108.3 MCF/H. RELEASE DURATION WAS UPDATED TO 30 MINUTES. WEATHER INFORMATION WAS UPDATED. 

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER STATED THAT A ZERO-TURN LAWN MOWER STRUCK A METER SET. BECAUSE OF THIS THE MOWER CAUSED A RELEASE AND IGNITION OF NATURAL GAS. DURING THIS INCIDENT THE OPERATOR RECEIVED UNSPECIFIED INJURIES AND WAS TRANSPORTED TO A NEARBY HOSPITAL FOR TREATMENT. THE PRICE POINT FOR DAMAGES IS EXPECTED TO BE AROUND (300,000) DOLLARS. THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED IS UNKNOWN TO THE CALLER. THE FIRE WAS EXTINGUISHED BY LOCAL AUTHORITIES

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470688///

UPDATE: AFTER ADDITIONAL CALCULATIONS, THE VOLUME IS ESTIMATED TO BE 60 BARRELS RATHER THAN 30. REMEDIATION IS IN PROGRESS. THE PIPELINE IS STILL ISOLATED.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF CRUDE OIL FROM A STEEL BELOW GROUND TRANSMISSION PIPELINE DUE TO UNKNOWN CAUSES.

///THIS IS 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470661///

UPDATE: REPAIRS ARE ONGOING, NO OTHER UPDATES TO PROVIDE.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY DISCOVERED A BALL OF ICE ON A TRANSMISSION LINE. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN TO THE CALLER. ACCORDING TO THE CALLER (8) GALLONS OF BUTANE RELEASED.

/// THIS IS AN PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470476 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THE EXPLOSION OF THE STRUCTURE DID NOT ORIGINATE FROM A SERVICE LINE AT THE LOCATION. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER REPORTED AN EXPLOSION AT A RESIDENTIAL BUILDING (DUPLEX) THAT  OCCURRED FOR UNKNOWN REASONS AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED  THERE HAS BEEN ONE CONFIRMED FATALITY. LIMITED INFORMATION WAS PROVIDED.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A 750FT CRUDE OIL TANKER VESSEL COLLIDED WITH A MULTI PURPOSE OFFSHORE SUPPLY VESSEL IN THE GULF IN AMERICA FOR UNKNOWN REASONS AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THERE IS AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF CRUDE OIL ONBOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY RELEASE. 

-NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470458 /// 

THE CALLER STATED THAT THERE IS NO UPDATE TO REPORT AT THIS TIME. ORIGINAL THE REPORT WAS LABELED AS FIXED, HOWEVER IT IS BEING CHANGED TO PIPELINE. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF NATURAL GAS, INTO THE ATMOSPHERE, FROM A REGULATOR AT THE PRIVATE RESIDENCE. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF  INCIDENT IS UNKNOWN, BUT SUSPECTED TO BE FROM A LIGHTNING STRIKE.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470461///

UPDATE: VOLUME OF RELEASED MATERIAL WAS UPDATED TO 150 GALLONS FROM 50 GALLONS. CONTACT INFORMATION FOR THE SRP WAS UPDATED. CLEAN UP IS COMPLETE AND SYSTEMS ARE BACK TO NORMAL

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER STATES WHILE OFFLOADING ETHANOL AT THE FACILITY, THEY OFFLOADED INTO A BLOCKED VALVE RESULTING IN A RELEASE OF 50 GALLONS OF ETHANOL TO SECONDARY CONTAINMENT.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470470 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT (255,000) MCF OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED DURING THE COURSE OF THIS INCIDENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER REPORTED A NATURAL GAS EXPLOSION AT A RESIDENTIAL HOME THAT  OCCURRED DUE TO TORNADOS THAT UPROOTED A SERVICE LINE AT THE INCIDENT  LOCATION. 

-ONE FATALITY.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470321 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE LEAK WAS IDENTIFIED AND A TEMPORARY CLAMP WAS INSTALLED. A PREEMINENT CLAMP WILL BE PLACED ON 08/14/2026. THE ONLY AFFECTED MEDIUM WAS SOIL. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF CRUDE OIL FROM A  PIPELINE, UNKNOWN CAUSE. SOIL STAINED, NO WATERWAY IMPACT.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1470011///

UPDATE: THE QUANTITY OF MATERIAL RELEASED WAS UPDATED TO 9.8 BARRELS. THE INCIDENT DURATION WAS 15 MINUTES AND ENDED AT 1430. NO DAMAGES OCCURRED.

ORIGINAL: NATURAL GASOLINE RELEASED FROM A PIPELINE VALVE BODY DUE TO MAINTENANCE ON THE VALVE WHILE REMOVING THE VALVE FITTING.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469972///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY INSTALLED A TEMPORARY PATCH. THERE HAS BEEN NO ADDITIONAL LEAKING FROM THE LINE. A PLIDCO CLAMP AND OTHER MATERIALS WILL ARRIVE ON 8/10/2026 FOR PERMANENT REPAIRS. THE QUALIFIED PERSONNEL WILL BE ON SITE ON 8/11/2026 OR 8/12/2026 FOR INSTALLATION OF THE PERMANENT REPAIRS. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

CRUDE OIL DISCHARGED FROM A 6 INCH PIPELINE DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT THIS TIME

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A 20FT PLEASURE CRAFT VESSEL IS PARTIALLY SUBMERGED IN INDIAN RIVER BAY WITH APPROXIMATELY 20 GALLONS OF GASOLINE, AND 5 QUARTS OF LUBRICANT OIL ON BOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY RELEASE. THE CAUSE OF THE VESSEL BECOMING SUBMERGED IS UNKNOWN. 

-ONE PERSON WAS RESCUED FROM THE VESSEL. NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469921 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THE CAUSE WAS ATTRIBUTED TO A FLANGE FAILURE. THE MATERIAL THAT RELEASED WAS RECOVERED AND IT WAS DISCOVERED THAT THE RQ WAS NOT MET. ACCORDING TO THE CALLER, (3429) POUNDS OF MATERIAL WERE RELEASED DURING THE INCIDENT.  

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

ALUMINUM SULFATE SOLUTION (COMMONLY REFERRED TO ALUM) RELEASED FROM A  SINGLE RAIL CAR DUE TO OPERATOR ERROR (A FLANGE WAS NOT PROPERLY  TIGHTENED).  THE RAIL CAR WAS NOT PART OF A TRAIN.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469827 ///

/// THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS ///

THE FIRE MARSHAL DETERMINED THAT THE EXPLOSION WAS CAUSED BY A RELEASE OF PROPANE. THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED A NATURAL GAS EXPLOSION AT A RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY DUE  TO UNKNOWN REASONS. (1) FATALITY AND (1) INJURY WERE REPORTED. THE CALLER  REPORTED A FIRE, BUT IT HAS BEEN EXTINGUISHED. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE, BUT THAT RELEASE  HAS BEEN SECURED. THE CALLER ALSO REPORTED A PROPANE TANK ON SITE THAT IS  STILL CURRENTLY LEAKING.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469686///

UPDATE: THE VESSEL IS STILL RELEASING MATERIAL AND HAS SUNKEN FURTHER INTO THE WATER. 

ORIGINAL: CALLER REPORTING A DERELICT VESSEL SINKING AT ITS MOORING, AND RELEASING AN UNKNOWN OIL. CALLER STATES THE VESSEL IS TIED TO ANOTHER DERELICT VESSEL. CALLER STATES THEY HAVE PICTURES.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469577 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE RESPONSIBLE PARTY HAS BEEN IDENTIFIED. THE EQUIPMENT WAS DETERMINED TO HAVE TWO 20 GALLON DIESEL TANKS AND ONE 25 GALLON HYDRAULIC OIL TANK, BUT IT IS STILL UNKNOWN IF THERE WAS ANY OIL INSIDE.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

CALLER REPORTING A PIECE OF MACHINERY UPSIDE DOWN IN THE RIVER. RESPONDERS  WITNESSED THE FUEL TANK ON THE MACHINERY IS OPEN, BUT IT IS NOT CONFIRMED  THAT ANY OIL RELEASED. THE CAUSE OF THE INCIDENT IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469577 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469625 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: UPON INVESTIGATION, IT WAS DETERMINED NO HAZARDOUS MATERIAL RELEASED. THE TRANSFORMER LANDED UPRIGHT AND THE LID DID NOT OPEN.

ORIGINAL UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER REPORTED A DISCHARGE OF APPROXIMATELY 16 GALLONS OF MINERAL OIL  (NON PCB) FROM A POLE TOP TRANSFORMER THAT WENT ONTO THE GROUND AND INTO  CABIN RUN (WATERWAY) AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CAUSE OF THE DISCHARGE  IS DUE TO A RECENT STORM THAT KNOCKED OVER THE POLE. 

-NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469625 ///

///THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT NUMBER 1469607. THE UPDATE IS THE RELEASE CAME FROM CUSTOMER PIPING. THERE WERE NO INJURIES AND THERE WERE NO FATALITIES./// 


///ORIGINAL///
THE CALLER RESPONDED TO A NATURAL GAS EXPLOSION.  INJURIES AND FATALITIES  AND UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME.  THE (2) NEIGHBORING RESIDENCES WERE EVACUATED  (AMOUNT OF PERSONS UNKNOWN).

AT THIS TIME PIPELINE HAS NOT BEEN RULED OUT AS THE CAUSE.

///VI WITH FIRE EXTINGUISHING WATER RELEASE TO STORM DRAIN | BC FERRIES | STRAIT OF GEORGIA | DELTA, BC  SWE - DGIR 262886///

DESCRIPTION OF SPILL SOURCE, CIRCUMSTANCES, CAUSE AND ADVERSE EFFECTS OF THE SPILL:
WATER USED TO EXTINGUISH A VEHICLE FIRE ESCAPED INTO A STORM DRAIN. AMOUNT THAT ESCAPED IS UNKNOWN.

///POTENTIAL RELEASE REPORT///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A POTENTIAL RELEASE OF GASOLINE, INTO LAKE ST CLAIR, FROM A PLEASURE CRAFT THAT HAD AN ENGINE EXPLODE AND CATCH FIRE. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE VESSEL EXPLODING IS UNKNOWN. CALLER STATES THAT (2) INDIVIDUALS WERE ON-BOARD, WERE RESCUED WITH (1) INJURED AND SENT TO THE HOSPITAL. 

CALLER STATES THE VESSEL HAS BEEN TIDE TO AN EMPTY SLIP AND WAS EXTINGUISHED BY ST CLAIR FIRE DEPARTMENT.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469323///

UPDATE: THE RELEASE WAS SECURED AT 0913. 

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A TUBING LEAK ON A FACILITY LINE RELEASED APPROX 10 POUNDS OF BUTADIENE INTO THE ATMOSPHERE. THIS RELEASE IS ONGOING. NO INJURIES OR EVACUATIONS REPORTED. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469330///

UPDATE:  TWO INDIVIDUALS WERE ATTEMPTING TO REMOVE PIPES FROM THE HOUSE IN AN ACT OF VANDALISM, TRIGGERING THE EXPLOSION.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING THAT SOMEONE LIT A LIGHTER IN A VACANT HOUSE AND CAUSED A SERVICE PIPELINE TO EXPLODE AND RELEASE AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS INTO THE ATMOSPHERE. 02 INJURIES REPORTED. SERVICE LINE WAS SECURED AND LOCAL FD RESPONDED TO SCENE. FIRE EXTINGUISHED AND INVESTIGATION IS ONGOING. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469395///

UPDATE: THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED AS OF1310.

ORIGINAL: UNKNOWN MATERIAL (POSSIBLY PROPANE, ETHANE OR METHANE) RELEASED FROM A PROCESS VENT DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT THIS TIME.  CALLER STATES THEY DISCOVERED THE RELEASE WHILE USING A FLARE CAMERA DOING A L-DAR SURVEY.

///THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1469231///

CORRECTION: THE SHEEN SIZE HAS BEEN CORRECTED TO 6 MILES BY 300 YARDS. CALLER ALSO STATED THAT ONBOARD SENSORS WERE CHECKED ON THEIR PLATFORM TO CONFIRM THAT THE MATERIAL WAS NOT COMING FROM IT.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING AN UNKNOWN SHEEN FROM AN UNKNOWN SOURCE IN THE GULF OFFSHORE. SHEEN DESCRIBED AS LIGHT GREY SPREADING 6 MILES X 30 YARDS MOVING SOUTHEAST. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469292///

UPDATED: THERE IS NO ADDITIONAL SHEENING AS OF TODAY, RELEASE IS SECURED, OPERATORS WILL CONTINUE TO MONITOR AND MAKE ANY NECESSARY REPAIRS.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER DISCOVERED A RELEASE OF CRUDE OIL FROM AN OUT-OF-SERVICE FLOW LINE IMPACTING THE GULF OF AMERICA.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469135 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE NUMBER OF DERAILED CARS FROM 51 TO 10. THE CAR NUMBERS WERE PROVIDED. THE CARS WERE LOADED WITH SOYBEAN MEAL, AND THERE WAS A RELEASE OF MATERIAL TO SOIL. THE AMOUNT RELEASED IS UNKNOWN. NO WATERWAYS WERE AFFECTED.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

TRAIN LWH30 27 UP8054 DERAILED 51 OF 52 RAILCARS IT WAS CARRYING ON THE  MAINLINE. NO INJURIES, RELEASES, OR HAZMAT IS INVOLVED.

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469179 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THE FIRE MARSHAL DETERMINED THAT NATURAL GAS WAS NOT RELEASED. BECAUSE OF THIS THE CALLER STATED THAT THE INCIDENT AS A WHOLE IS NOT REPORTABLE. THE CALLER STATED THAT THERE WAS NO RELEASE OF MATERIAL THAT OCCURRED. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///  

THE CALLER STATED THAT NATURAL GAS RELEASED FROM A FLEX HOSE FOR AN  APPLIANCE AT THE LOCATION. BECAUSE OF THIS, A FIRE WAS IGNITED AT THE  LOCATION. THE PRICE POINT FOR DAMAGES IS EXPECTED TO EXCEED (153700)  DOLLARS. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS UNKNOWN AND UNDER INVESTIGATION BY  LOCAL AUTHORITIES. THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED HAS YET TO BE  DETERMINE

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469191 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT BENZENE HAS ALSO BEEN RELEASED IN UNKNOWN AMOUNTS. ALTHOUGH THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED IS UNKNOWN, THE CALLER SUSPECTS GREATER THAN (10) POUNDS MAY HAVE RELEASED. 


/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATED THAT HYDROGEN SULFIDE RELEASED FROM AN UNKNOWN SOURCE AT A REFINERY. THE MATERIAL RELEASED INTO THE ATMOSPHERE IN UNKNOWN AMOUNTS.  ALTHOUGH THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT RELEASED IS UNKNOWN, THE CALLER  SUSPECTS UPWARDS OF (100) POUNDS MAY HAVE RELEASED.

/// THIS IS A UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469202 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT (232.6) POUNDS OF AMMONIA RELEASED DURING THIS INCIDENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATES DUE TO HEAVY STORMS THE POWER WAS OUT AT THE FACILITY.   CREWS DISCOVERED A PRESSURE RELIEF VALVE POPPED OFF AND RELEASED ANHYDROUS  AMMONIA.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1469158///

UPDATED: CALLER REPORTED THAT AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED UNDERGROUND AS A GAS TO AIR. IT IS STILL UNDER INVESTIGATION WHETHER ANY MATERIAL RELEASED ABOVE THE GROUND. A SMALL SECTION OF SUNSET BLVD IS CLOSED IN ALL DIRECTIONS. A SECTION OF THE PIPE WAS CUT AND CAPPED AND MATERIAL IS NO LONGER FLOWING THROUGH THE PIPE. THEY ARE STILL PERFORMING LEAK CHECKS, MONITORING AND SIPHONING GAS FROM THE GROUND, AND PERFORMING ADVANCED LEAK PROTECTION SURVEYS.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN MATERIAL, OIL, AND GAS FROM A STRUCTURE FIRE AT A TAVERN. THE CALLER STATES THAT IT IS UNKNOWN IF THE FIRE IS NATURAL GAS AT THIS TIME. CALLER STATES THAT THERE MAY BE (1) INJURED PARTY TRANSPORTED TO THE NEAREST HOSPITAL. CALLER STATES THAT THE FIRE DEPARTMENT ON SCENE PUT A 500 FT EVACUATION RADIUS IN PLACE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469153 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE MATERIAL RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE HYDRAULIC OIL.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF GEAR OIL, INTO ALLIGATOR BAYOU, FROM  USV 1001. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS EQUIPMENT  MALFUNCTION ON THE LOWER STERN DRIVE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1469153 ///

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR UPDATE TO REPORT 1469005 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: UPON INVESTIGATION, THE PIPE THAT RELEASED THE GAS WAS DETERMINED TO BE NON-JURISDICTIONAL PIPING, SO THIS EVENT WAS NOT REPORTABLE.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS FROM A  DISCHARGE PIPELINE DUE TO A RUPTURE. THE INCIDENT IS REPORTABLE DUE TO  DAMAGE AMOUNT.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR UPDATE TO REPORT 1469005 ///

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///  

THE CALLER REPORTED TWO BARGES COLLIDED FOR UNKNOWN REASONS IN THE INTERCOASTAL WATERWAY AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THERE IS AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF VACUUM GAS OIL ON BOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY RELEASE. 

-BOTH BARGES WERE DAMAGED. LIMITED INFORMATION WAS PROVIDED.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THAT AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF 'HYDROGEN PHOSPHIDE' (FUMIGANT) MAY OR MAY NOT HAVE RELEASED TO ATMOSPHERE (WITHIN THE CARGO HOLD) DUE TO REACTING WITH WATER WHICH IGNITED INTO A SMALL PALM SIZED FIRE.

SOURCE OF WATER IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME.


/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

////////THIS IS A CORRECTION FOR NRC REPORT NUMBER 1468814.  INCORRECT COUNTY WAS PROVIDED.  THE CORRECT COUNTY IS ST. LAWRENCE.////////

ORIGINAL REPORT:
LUBE OIL DISCHARGED FROM A JOURNAL BEARING OF A HYDRO-ELECTRIC GENERATOR  DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT THIS TIME.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


USCG RECEIVED AN EMAIL FROM THE HARBORMASTER WHO RECEIVED AN EMAIL FROM A BOATER STATING THAT AN UNKNOWN ENTITY DEPARTED THE' WAIANAE BOAT HARBOR' AND  PURPOSEFULLY SANK THE SAILING VESSEL 'DOUBLE TROUBLE' IN 'POKA'I BAY' FOR UNKNOWN REASONS.


/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO REPORT 1468869 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THERE ARE NO SIGNIFICANT UPDATES TO PASS.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER REPORTED THAT DURING MAINTENANCE ACTIVITIES OF AN ABOVEGROUND  TRANSMISSION PIPELINE, A FLASH FIRE OCCURRED. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE  OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF CRUDE OIL VAPORS.

/// THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO REPORT 1468869 ///

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1468653///

UPDATE: RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. THE INCIDENT WAS CAUSED BY A PINHOLE LEAK IN FACILITY PIPING. AMOUNT OF BENZENE RELEASED UPDATED TO 38 POUNDS. CALLER ALSO A REPORTED A RELEASE OF 300 POUNDS OF PARAXYLENE. AREA HAS BEEN CLEANED UP AND CALLER REPORTED THAT NO HITS OCCURRED ON THEIR AIR MONITORING.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF BENZENE TO THE AIR AT REFINERY DUE TO UNKNOWN CAUSES.

/// THIS IS A SECOND UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1468655 ///

THE CALLER UPDATED THE RELEASE AMOUNTS TO 43.13 POUNDS OF BENZENE, 13,978.55 POUNDS OF METHANE, 2,326.2 POUNDS OF VOCS, 68.84 POUNDS OF TOLUENE, 2.66 POUNDS OF ETHYLBENZENE, AND 35.62 POUNDS OF TOTAL XYLENE. THERE WAS NO REPORTED ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT. 

/// FIRST UPDATE BELOW ///

UPDATED INFO:
- THE RELEASE HAS ENDED AT 2131.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT 1468588 BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED THAT THE THERMAL OXIDIZERS TRIPPED AT AN LNG FACILITY.  THIS CAUSED THE FACILITY TO ROUTE ACID GAS TO A RECOVERY UNIT.  AN UNKNOWN  FAILURE CAUSED A RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF ACID GAS INTO THE   ATMOSPHERE FROM FACILITY PIPING.

///  THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1468460 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT (2.7) MMCF OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED DURING THE COURSE OF THIS INCIDENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW. 

CALLER IS REPORTING A THIRD PARTY STRUCK AN UNDERGROUND 8-INCH TRANSMISSION PIPELINE AND RELEASED .507 MCF OF NATURAL GAS. NO INJURIES OR EVACUATIONS  REPORTED. NO CLEAN UP EFFORTS REPORTED. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1468327 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF HYDROGEN FLUORIDE RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE 25.4 POUNDS, WHICH IS UNDER THE REPORTABLE QUANTITY.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS:

/// THIS REPORT IS RELATED TO NRC REPORT 1468317 ///

CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF ANHYDROUS HYDROGEN FLUORIDE FROM A RAIL CAR ON THE FACILITY. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN. RELEASE   ONGOING. THE RAIL CAR IS OWNED BY THE FACILITY, BUT CAME IN ON A NORFOLK  SOUTHERN TRAIN.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1468327 ///

/// THIS IS A PHMSA 48-HOUR UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1468373 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE PIPE HAS BEEN RETURNED TO SERVICE. THE CALLER STATED THAT (10663) MCF OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED DURING THIS INCIDENT. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 


THE CALLER STATED THAT A LOW MAINTENANCE ROAD WAS BEING GRADED BY A THIRD  PARTY, WHEN A PIPELINE AT THE LOCATION WAS STRUCK. BECAUSE OF THIS AN  UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED INTO THE ATMOSPHERE. CURRENTLY  STATUS OF DAMAGES IS UNKNOWN TO THE CALLER.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT NUMBER 1468288. THE UPDATE IS THAT THE RELEASE ORIGINATED FROM THE PIPELINE UNDERGROUND, THE AMOUNT OF RELEASE IS 3800 BARRELS AND THE MATERIAL IS CONTAINED.///

///ORIGINAL///
THE CALLER STATES THAT AN UNKNOWN LOCAL FIRE DEPARTMENT DISCOVERED A  RELEASE OF DIESEL, INTO THE YARD, FROM AN ABOVE GROUND VALVE ON AND  UNDERGROUND 36" TRANSMISSION PIPELINE AT THE BOOSTER STATION. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

////THIS IS A 48 HOUR PHMSA UPDATE TO REPORT #1468312////

UPDATE IS AS FOLLOW:
SYSTEM BACK IN SERVICE

////PREVIOUS REPORTS///

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT NUMBER 1468288. THE UPDATE IS THAT THE  RELEASE ORIGINATED FROM THE PIPELINE UNDERGROUND, THE AMOUNT OF RELEASE IS  3800 BARRELS AND THE MATERIAL IS CONTAINED.///

///ORIGINAL///
THE CALLER STATES THAT AN UNKNOWN LOCAL FIRE DEPARTMENT DISCOVERED A   RELEASE OF DIESEL, INTO THE YARD, FROM AN ABOVE GROUND VALVE ON AND   UNDERGROUND 36" TRANSMISSION PIPELINE AT THE BOOSTER STATION. THE CALLER  STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THEY RECEIVED A REPORT OF A SUNKEN VESSEL IN SHALLOW WATER IN THE MORADA BAY ANCHORAGE AREA.

02 ENGINES ON BOARD; TYPE/AMOUNT OF POTENTIAL RELEASE IS UNKNOWN.

NO SHEEN REPORTED AT THIS TIME


